Worked films (skills/video-decompiler/library/films)

  plusone/media/art: crops of public-domain works from the open-access collections of the Metropolitan Museum of Art,
  the Art Institute of Chicago and the Cleveland Museum of Art, each flagged public domain or CC0 in the museum's own
  record. Titles, artists, museums and links: plusone/media/art/SOURCES.md.

  plusone/media/fonts: Fraunces, Playfair Display, Anton, Bricolage Grotesque and DM Serif Display, each under the SIL
  Open Font License 1.1 (the licence texts are beside the files). Geist and Geist Mono (Vercel, SIL Open Font License
  1.1) are embedded in each film's kit/fonts.gen.ts; their licence texts are in each film's media/fonts.

  onoma/media/fonts/Geist-VF.ttf: Geist (Vercel), the same font onoma/kit/fonts.gen.ts embeds, kept as a file for
  onoma/tools/glyphs.py. SIL Open Font License 1.1; the licence text is beside it.

  linden/media/art: crops and reductions of public-domain works from the open-access collections of the
  Metropolitan Museum of Art, the Art Institute of Chicago and the Cleveland Museum of Art, each flagged public
  domain or CC0 in the museum's own record. Titles, makers, museums and links: linden/media/art/SOURCES.md.

  linden/media/fonts: Fraunces and Bricolage Grotesque, each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, with Geist and
  Geist Mono embedded in linden/kit/fonts.gen.ts (Vercel, SIL Open Font License 1.1); the licence texts are beside
  the files.

  linden/media/sounds: recorded instruments, each folder with its LICENCE.txt. Salamander Grand Piano V2 by
  Alexander Holm, CC BY 3.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/), via github.com/Tonejs/audio. Pizzicato
  strings from the FluidR3_GM soundfont by Frank Wen, rendered by Benjamin Gleitzman
  (github.com/gleitz/midi-js-soundfonts), CC BY 3.0. Vibraphone and glockenspiel from the Versilian Community Sample
  Library (github.com/sgossner/VCSL, Versilian Studios), CC0; their WAV files are stored as FLAC, losslessly. A film
  made with the piano or the strings owes their credit wherever it is published.
